    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A skilled actress secretly Embraced by João Bilé, Margarida Cordeiro was planted undercover as an anarch Toreador, reporting back to her true sire only via dead drops and never meeting him openly. Over time she has embraced her cover identity's recklessness fully &mdash; so fully that she has committed diablerie without her sire's knowledge, a secret that could unravel Bilé's entire scheme if it ever surfaced.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Play Margarida as a genuinely gifted performer who has started to lose the line between her Toreador cover and her real self, reckless and thrill-seeking in ways that unsettle even her fellow anarchs. She hides a dangerous secret &mdash; her diablerie &mdash; extremely well, but it colors her hunger and her instability underneath the charming exterior.</p><p><strong>Disciplines (as printed, dot-rating, convert to owned Discipline Items at Storyteller discretion):</strong> Celerity 1, Presence 2, Fortitude 3.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: João Bilé (secret; contact only via dead drops). Embrace: 1993. Undercover as an anarch Toreador. Has committed diablerie without her sire's knowledge. Part of Sample Brood: Bilé's Gambit, Clanbook: Ventrue, Chapter Three.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
